  299, 399, 80, 'plants/money-plant.jpg',
  4.9, 528, 'India’s favourite houseplant. Grows in water, soil, sun or shade.', 'The Money Plant is the reason a lot of people become plant people. It roots from a cutting in a glass of water, trails metres across a wall, and quietly filters formaldehyde and benzene from the air while doing it.', 'Cut just below a node and root it in water — that is a free new plant in three weeks.',
  'toxic', 'Easy', 'low', 'medium',
  'Very Low', 'Fast', 'Trails to 3 m',
  'Anything from low light to bright indirect. More light means more variegation.', 'Weekly. Let the top 3 cm dry out first.', 'Any general potting mix — or plain water in a bottle.', 'Tolerates dry air well.',
  '15–30 °C.', 'Monthly balanced feed in spring and summer.', 'Every 1–2 years, or just take cuttings and start again.',
  TRUE, TRUE
