  1299, 1649, 12, 'plants/staghorn-fern.jpg',
  4.6, 63, 'A living sculpture that grows on a board instead of in a pot.', 'An epiphyte, so in the wild it clings to trees rather than soil. Mounted on wood it becomes wall art with antler-shaped fronds. Unusual, pet safe, and a real conversation piece.', 'The flat brown shield fronds at the base are meant to look dead. Never remove them.',
  'safe', 'Moderate', 'medium', 'medium',
  'Medium', 'Slow', '45–90 cm spread',
  'Bright indirect light. No direct afternoon sun.', 'Soak the mount in water for 10 minutes weekly, then let it drain fully.', 'None — mount on wood with sphagnum moss, or use a very loose orchid mix.', 'High. Mist several times a week, or hang it in a bathroom.',
  '16–27 °C.', 'Diluted feed once a month in spring and summer.', 'Re-mount every 3–5 years as the shield fronds spread.',
  FALSE, FALSE
