  649, 849, 32, 'plants/bougainvillea.jpg',
  4.7, 205, 'A wall of magenta on a terrace that gets punishing sun.', 'Nothing else gives this much colour for this little water. Bougainvillea flowers hardest when it is hot, dry and slightly neglected - a genuinely drought-tolerant plant for the harshest spot on your terrace.', 'Too much water and feed gives a green bush with no colour. Treat it mean.',
  'caution', 'Easy', 'high', 'low',
  'Low', 'Fast', '1-3 m',
  'Full direct sun, 6+ hours. Shade means leaves and no colour.', 'Every 5-7 days. Letting it dry between waterings triggers flowering.', 'Ordinary well-draining soil. It does not want richness.', 'Low to moderate.',
  '20-38 C.', 'Low-nitrogen, high-potassium feed monthly in the growing season.', 'Every 2-3 years. A snug pot means more flowers.',
  FALSE, FALSE
